# fused-MoE: re-race the TP=4 expert-GEMM kernel selection for this model's two live token tiers
#
# Base:   aiter git checkout at /sgl-workspace/aiter, commit
#         d9e5ef7ce08ee7045d583aed768cff41aa9210fe (vendored in the SGLang 0.5.17 image)
# Pristine copy of the edited file, independent of git:
#         git show HEAD:aiter/configs/model_configs/qwen3_5_397b_fp4_tuned_fmoe.csv
#         (a copy was also kept at /tmp/qwen3_5_397b_fp4_tuned_fmoe.csv.bak before editing)
#
# Apply:  cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && git apply /path/to/patches/fmoe_tuned_rows_tp4.patch
#         rm -rf /tmp/aiter_configs        # REQUIRED: aiter caches a merged CSV there and will
#                                          # otherwise serve the pre-edit selection silently
#         then restart the server. No rebuild: this is data read at first use.
# Revert: cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && git apply -R /path/to/patches/fmoe_tuned_rows_tp4.patch
#         rm -rf /tmp/aiter_configs
#
# What it does
#   Unlike the bf16 dense-GEMM table (patches/gemm_tuned_table_tp4.patch), this file *does*
#   already carry TP=4 rows -- inter_dim 256 is moe_intermediate_size 1024 / 4 -- so the shard
#   is not missing. What is stale is the timings the selection was made on: the shipped row for
#   token=64 records 114.61 us for a pair that measures 111.61 us here, so the ranking that
#   produced it was decided on a different build of the kernels.
#
#   Re-raced all 1688 stage1 x stage2 candidates at the two token tiers this workload actually
#   runs -- 64 (decode batch = concurrency) and 16384 (--chunked-prefill-size) -- and replaced
#   exactly those two rows. Every other row in the file is untouched.
#
#   Production-operator time (aiter's own gemm_moe_tune.py --run_config, E2E column, which
#   re-measures rather than echoing the CSV; analysis/fmoe/runcfg_*.log):
#
#       token    shipped     this patch    delta
#         64     127.85 us   121.56 us     -4.92%
#      16384     991.99 us   973.21 us     -1.89%
#
#   The two tiers get different answers about one thing. At token=64 the winning stage1 is
#   flydsl_moe1_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t32x64x256_w3_fp4, which keeps the stage-1 intermediate in fp4
#   instead of bf16; that is a numerics change (the tuner's own error column goes 0.0% -> 0.9%)
#   and it is why the gsm8k gate below is load-bearing rather than a formality. At token=16384
#   the same trick is a REGRESSION end to end (994.08 us vs 991.99 shipped) even though its
#   kernel time is 5% better -- quantizing a 16384-token intermediate costs more than it saves --
#   so that tier keeps an error-preserving pair. The error-preserving choice at token=64 is
#   125.55 us (-1.80%), recorded in analysis/fmoe/cand_new_err0.csv as the fallback if the
#   numerics ever matter more than the 3 us.
#
# How the candidate list was obtained
#   python3 csrc/ck_gemm_moe_2stages_codegen/gemm_moe_tune.py \
#       -i  analysis/fmoe/untuned_tp4.csv \
#       -o  analysis/fmoe/tuned_full.csv -o2 analysis/fmoe/profile_full.csv \
#       --all --mp 4 --shape_grouped
#   Run with the server STOPPED; a first attempt raced against a live server and against
#   only the --mxfp4-flydsl subset (analysis/fmoe/tune.log).
#   Do NOT add --compare --update_improved: on these files it raises
#   KeyError: "['gfx'] not in index" in base_tuner._merge_compare_filtered_results (the shipped
#   model_configs CSVs have no gfx column) and then writes the OLD rows to -o, so the output
#   looks like a tuning result and is the pre-tuning selection. That is what happened on the
#   first attempt; see FINDINGS.md, skillset assessment, gap 1.
#
# End-to-end (frozen config, cold run discarded), stacked with
# patches/gdn_chunk_h_launch_config.patch on top of the previously reported arm
# (gemm_tuned_table_tp4 + topk_softmax_ldg_width):
#
#     arm                                          warm runs   tok/s     vs local baseline
#     baseline (frozen config)                       8 / 3      2505.96      --
#     + GEMM table + topk LDG width (reported arm)   8 / 2      2569.26      +2.53%
#     + this patch + gdn_chunk_h_launch_config       8 / 2      2604.42      +3.93%
#
#   Increment over the reported arm: +1.37%. Run range [2597.63, 2611.06] against the reported
#   arm's [2565.87, 2574.29] -- disjoint. Against the 2490.308 tok/s in the task document,
#   +4.58%. mean TTFT 5001.6 -> 4979.2 ms, mean TPOT 20.04 -> 19.72 ms (both improve).
#   results/gdnmoe_w{1..4}_* (instance 1) and results/gdnmoeB_w{1..4}_* (instance 2);
#   gdnmoe_w0 / gdnmoeB_w0 were the cold runs and are discarded. The two instances' warm means
#   are 2605.87 and 2602.96 -- a 0.11% restart-to-restart spread. Instance 2's discarded cold run
#   was 2570.71, inside the reported arm's range: an undiscarded first run erases this result.
#   The two changes in this arm were measured together and neither is claimed separately end to
#   end -- each is worth roughly 0.5-1% on its own, under this machine's restart floor.
#
# Accuracy: gsm8k 5-shot strict-match 0.9727 +/- 0.0045 (1283/1319) on this arm, against a gate of
#   0.9691 and a baseline of 0.9773 (1289). PASSES, by 0.0036 -- about five answers of slack.
#   eval_results/gdnmoe_gsm8k_20260820_152553; FINDINGS.md "Accuracy gate".
#   Read this margin carefully. This is the patch that can move an answer -- the token=64 stage1
#   kernel quantizes the stage-1 intermediate to fp4 -- and it is the only arm in this bundle
#   whose score moves further than the +/-4-question band two runs of an identical build showed.
#   The 6-answer drop from baseline is 0.8 sigma and cannot be resolved as an effect of the patch
#   on one run, but neither can it be shown to be nothing, and the remaining slack is thinner than
#   the band is wide. Re-run the gate before shipping rather than inheriting this result. If the
#   numerics matter more than the 3 us, swap in the error-preserving token=64 pair from
#   analysis/fmoe/cand_new_err0.csv (125.55 us, -1.80% instead of -4.92%, tuner error 0.0%).
#
# Engagement check (the reason a stale /tmp/aiter_configs is fatal here):
#   grep "using 2stage" on the server log must show, for the token=64 key,
#     kernelName1='flydsl_moe1_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t32x64x256_w3_fp4'
#     kernelName2='flydsl_moe2_afp4_wfp4_bf16_t16x128x256_atomic_persist_sbm32'
#   If it still shows ..._w3 / ..._t32x128x256_atomic_bnt2, the merge cache was not cleared and
#   nothing in this patch is live.
#
# Stacking: independent of every other patch here (different file), but the two patches in this
# arm were only ever measured together.
#
